What a person reads when the download and external-application seam refuses.

The set is derived one-for-one from the decision enums that already exist in
//taffy/common/public/taffy_download_intent.h: `DownloadDecision` and
`ExternalIntentDecision`. That is deliberate. A refusal the browser process
can return and cannot explain is a refusal a person experiences as a bug, so
the catalogue is complete against the enum rather than against a screen that
does not exist yet. `kAllowOrdinaryPath` needs no string in either enum: it is
Chromium's ordinary path, prompts and all.

Wording rules, from docs/voice-and-naming.md and docs/product/brand.md: the
product is TaffyGo and the assistant is Taffy, never interchangeably; the
assistant is "it"; a refusal says what happened and what the person can do
next; nothing here claims to be security UI.
-->
<grit-part>
  <message name="IDS_TAFFY_DOWNLOAD_REFUSED_UNATTRIBUTED"
           desc="Shown when a download was stopped because the browser could not attribute what started it. This is a fail-closed refusal: the person did nothing wrong and can start the download themselves.">
    TaffyGo could not tell what started this download, so it stopped it. Tap the download link again to start it yourself.
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_TAFFY_DOWNLOAD_REFUSED_ASSISTANT"
           desc="Shown when the assistant tried to start a download. The assistant has no download capability at all, so this states a rule rather than reporting a failure.">
    Taffy cannot start downloads. Download the file yourself if you want it.
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_TAFFY_DOWNLOAD_REFUSED_NO_LEASE"
           desc="Shown when a download was attributed to an assistant task that is not currently working in this tab.">
    Taffy is not working in this tab, so this download did not start.
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_TAFFY_EXTERNAL_INTENT_KEPT_IN_BROWSER"
           desc="Shown when a link that would normally open a different app was opened in the browser instead, because no installed app handles it. Information, not a refusal.">
    No app on this device opens that link, so TaffyGo opened it here.
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_TAFFY_EXTERNAL_INTENT_REFUSED_UNATTRIBUTED"
           desc="Shown when handing a link to another app was stopped because the browser could not attribute what asked for it.">
    TaffyGo could not tell what asked to open another app, so it stopped. Tap the link again to open it yourself.
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_TAFFY_EXTERNAL_INTENT_REFUSED_ASSISTANT"
           desc="Shown when the assistant tried to hand a link to another app. The assistant has no capability to leave the browser.">
    Taffy cannot open other apps. Tap the link yourself if you want to leave TaffyGo.
  </message>
</grit-part>
